// 13. (DEF-342, the ACCEPTED OVER-REFUSAL, management 2026-10-29 09:57:24) the callee writes the DISJOINT field `k` through the copy while the caller views `o`: the copy's write is recorded at the pointee's WHOLE extent (the store road's design since landing 156), so the call is refused; 0 tree sites
func:accepted_over_refusal_disjoint_field_through_copy = NIL() never fails {
    H2:h = H2{ o: string_concat("ab", "cd"), k: 1i64 };
    H2->:hp = @h;
    fixed uint8[]:vw = string_bytes(h.o);
    drop wrk(hp);
    discard(vw[0i64] => int32);
    pass NIL;
};

// 14. (DEF-341's `any->` face, the REVERSE laundering, f9j6c) a plain pointer parameter copied into an `any->` local and
// written through the local's cast back, the caller viewing the pointee
func:plain_param_laundered_through_any_local = NIL() never fails {
    H2:h = H2{ o: string_concat("ab", "cd"), k: 1i64 };
    H2->:hp = @h;
